{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"850779383656218636","content":"meanwhile shout out to UPS - the package with Crui's meds has been in a warehouse for like a week now, I call them today, I get voice recognition bot, that isn't even done well. first attempt, I find the (not mentioned by the automatic messages - pressing 0 on the keyboard, keep that in mind for later) option to skip it and connect to a human. after 15 minutes on hold I hang up. I try again after a few minutes, this time letting the machine see what it can do. it wants you to say the tracking number out loud. you can type it in if it only has digits, but of course it doesn't. the last 8 digits of it are four zeroes and four other stuff. midway through me saying every zero, **it apparently instead decides to interpret the zeroes as redirect to a human**","created_at":"2021-08-17T13:16:52.792000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877179176136896512","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
